# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/
.swc

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# test/verification artifacts (Playwright test runner + MCP browser tool)
/test-results/
/.screenshots/
/.playwright-mcp/

# Cloud sync per-replica local state (manifest baseline + conflict log)
**/.cloud-sync-*

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.local.example
!.env.test.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.superpowers/

# Transient scheduled-task lock (per-session runtime artifact)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# dev error log (runtime observability artifact — never commit)
/logs/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (permission grants, local paths) — not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

/.cache/

# Agent working detritus (codex task output, session scratch)
.codex-tasks/
scratchpad/
dist/

# Python bytecode. scripts/codex-review.py imports scripts/codex-frontier-model.py, so a
# __pycache__/ appears under scripts/ on every review dispatch (PR #27).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# jest --json output, produced by CI for scripts/check-test-counts.py and handy locally.
jest-results.json

# Playwright auth state + seeded fixture for the cloud e2e (regenerated by the setup project)
playwright/.auth/

# Post-Plan Gate sentinel — transient, per-working-copy. Armed by
# .claude/hooks/check-plan-gate.sh, cleared at Post-Plan Gate 5/5.
.claude/plan-gate-pending

# Session-local execution state, armed by .claude/hooks/block-idle-stop.sh. Names the plan being
# executed and the last blocked step-count; both are per-machine, per-session. The PLAN's checkboxes
# are the durable, committed record of progress — these two files only decide when to interrupt.
.claude/executing-plan
.claude/executing-plan.state

# Session plans written by scripts/begin-plan.py. Deliberately NOT in docs/superpowers/plans/:
# that directory is the anchor registry's population (check-anchors.py globs it and requires a
# Goal + Anchor header on every dated file) and it is the durable design corpus. A session to-do
# list is neither — it is per-machine execution state, like the two sentinels above.
.claude/plans/

# Warn-only firings of scripts/check-banner-armed.py — one tab-separated line per turn that
# announced `## ▶ STEP i of N` with nothing armed. Per-machine evidence, not a shared record: it
# exists so the decision to promote that check from warning to blocking rests on a COUNT rather
# than an impression.
.claude/banner-warnings.log

# Which commit a CI watcher is armed for (scripts/check-ci-watched.py). SHA-scoped on purpose:
# a new push moves HEAD, the sentinel stops matching, and the check warns again. "Armed once,
# covered forever" is the bug it exists to catch, not the behaviour it should have.
.claude/ci-watching

# Generated pages never belong at the repo root. MEASURED 2026-08-30: `frag.html`
# and `rel-nested.html` — two rendered dashboards — were committed in 96ae502 by
# `git add -A`. They were written by the round-4 breach sweep, which applies every
# mutation entry INCLUDING the two whose whole point is a RELATIVE `--out` /
# `--fragment-only` path, and which did not pin its cwd. `--mutate .` itself is
# safe (`run_suite` uses `cwd=<temp copy>`); the hazard is an instrument run from
# the repo root. This is a backstop, not the fix — the fix is that instruments
# pin their cwd.
/*.html
